      "writtenOn": "2022-11-15T02:30:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I didn\u0027t know such files, thanks! However I think we don\u0027t need to check inside for measuring guest_time.\n\nI compared data between `/proc/\u003cpid\u003e/stat` and `/proc/\u003cpid\u003e/task/*/stat`, the guest_time of crosvm_vcpu0 was same with the guest_time of entire crosvm process.\nhttps://screenshot.googleplex.com/AaZCidCGAAWZGnE\n\nFYI, definition of guest_time (https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man5/proc.5.html) : Guest time of the process (time spent running a virtual CPU for a guest operating system), measured in clock ticks (divide by sysconf(_SC_CLK_TCK)).\n\nBy the way, the way you suggested seems quite helpful for checking utime and stime which gaves user/kernel time info in given pid/tid, but I still think guest_time information is closer to our thoughts. HDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "75579a01_e62aa0c8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 444,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 444,
        "endChar": 86
